Z||000003||AusFiero||04-23-2001||04:48 AM||||I found a 1988 GT with t-tops once with 6000 mls on the clock. Had been stored since 1987. Rang up about it getting ready to jump on a plane to the states ASAP and had missed it by 3 hours  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> . It had been on the market for 3 months prior and was $6000 US. I ended up buying my 1986 GT Fastback with t-tops locally.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||05-06-2001||10:30 AM||||Ok!!! It's finally official and the car is sitting in my garage! It's a white Formula with 80,000 km (50,000 miles). A/c, 5 spd, tan interior (oh well, you can't always get exactly what you want) and I picked it up for the sceaming price of $3500 Canadian (that's like $2500US) After missing out on so many others, and having looked at so many junkers with outrageous price tags, I can't believe my luck at finding such a fine example for such a good price. Yahoo, now the fun begins!||||reg||1
